1
00:00:06,621 --> 00:00:08,443
Listen to rain on a roof.

2
00:00:08,523 --> 00:00:10,250
Every drop is different.

3
00:00:10,330 --> 00:00:14,761
The sound swells, thins, and
changes as the wind changes.

4
00:00:14,841 --> 00:00:17,551
It is vivid, and it never holds still.

5
00:00:18,361 --> 00:00:23,946
Now try to say exactly what you heard.
The words come out flat. Rain. A sound.

6
00:00:24,026 --> 00:00:25,699
Loud, then soft.

7
00:00:25,779 --> 00:00:27,959
What you heard was far richer than that.

8
00:00:28,757 --> 00:00:33,871
This is After Anatta: notes by
John Tan, known as Thusness.

9
00:00:34,702 --> 00:00:38,889
The difficulty in presenting this
view is not mainly in the view.

10
00:00:38,969 --> 00:00:44,215
It is in the tools. Words, concepts
and drawings were made for daily life.

11
00:00:44,295 --> 00:00:49,364
Lifting a cup. Catching a bus. Keeping
a promise. For that they work well.

12
00:00:49,444 --> 00:00:52,448
A cup must stay a cup
long enough to be filled.

13
00:00:52,528 --> 00:00:55,184
A friend must be the same friend tomorrow.

14
00:00:56,018 --> 00:00:59,539
But turned on what actually
appears, the tools are clumsy.

15
00:00:59,619 --> 00:01:01,183
And there is a worse problem.

16
00:01:01,263 --> 00:01:04,539
A tool that cannot show
something does not stay silent.

17
00:01:04,619 --> 00:01:07,976
It shows something else
instead, shaped like the tool.

18
00:01:08,056 --> 00:01:11,568
Not knowing the limits of our
tools shapes what we present.

19
00:01:12,417 --> 00:01:14,362
Three things make the trouble plain.

20
00:01:14,442 --> 00:01:16,427
What appears is vivid and moving.

21
00:01:16,507 --> 00:01:18,601
It is not found when looked for.

22
00:01:18,681 --> 00:01:22,070
And it follows its conditions.
It is not haphazard.

23
00:01:22,869 --> 00:01:24,541
Start with the vividness.

24
00:01:24,621 --> 00:01:28,400
A concept works by picking
out: this, not that.

25
00:01:28,480 --> 00:01:31,308
It gives a thing edges
and keeps it the same.

26
00:01:31,388 --> 00:01:34,582
But no sound is ever the same sound twice.

27
00:01:34,662 --> 00:01:37,965
A wall is one colour at
noon and another at dusk.

28
00:01:38,045 --> 00:01:42,535
A tool made for picking out steady things
cannot show what never stands still.

29
00:01:43,372 --> 00:01:49,012
Here is the first trap. It is tempting to
say: underneath the concepts there is raw,

30
00:01:49,092 --> 00:01:53,346
vivid experience, and the
concepts are a thin layer on top.

31
00:01:53,426 --> 00:01:55,017
That brings the floor back.

32
00:01:55,097 --> 00:01:57,572
There is no bare layer
waiting to be named.

33
00:01:57,652 --> 00:02:02,151
Whatever appears is already picked
out as this, before any word.

34
00:02:02,231 --> 00:02:07,137
So the poverty of the tools is not a gap
between words and a truer world behind

35
00:02:07,217 --> 00:02:11,498
them. The tools fit their job and
hold much less than what is there.

36
00:02:11,578 --> 00:02:15,507
And the actual mistake starts only when
a word is taken to have caught the thing

37
00:02:15,587 --> 00:02:16,787
itself.

38
00:02:17,405 --> 00:02:22,039
Now the conditions. The bell rings
when it is struck, not otherwise.

39
00:02:22,119 --> 00:02:23,751
Rice seed gives rice.

40
00:02:23,831 --> 00:02:26,609
This order is what makes
the world workable.

41
00:02:27,430 --> 00:02:31,648
But as soon as we say it, cause
and effect turns into production.

42
00:02:31,765 --> 00:02:34,687
First the conditions, then
something made out of them,

43
00:02:34,767 --> 00:02:36,539
like goods from a factory.

44
00:02:37,357 --> 00:02:39,899
Nagarjuna refuses exactly that.

45
00:02:39,979 --> 00:02:43,540
Cause has three senses,
and only one is refused.

46
00:02:43,620 --> 00:02:48,391
A cause that exists on its own and
hands over an effect is refused.

47
00:02:48,471 --> 00:02:53,961
Conditions that come together, so that
a result appears, are kept. That works.

48
00:02:54,041 --> 00:02:58,798
And the cause is the part attention picks
out when it lays a process out in order.

49
00:02:58,878 --> 00:03:00,515
That is all a cause is.

50
00:03:01,350 --> 00:03:04,504
So show the conditions as
the shape of the appearing,

51
00:03:04,584 --> 00:03:07,615
not a machine behind it. A bell is struck.

52
00:03:07,695 --> 00:03:11,202
Bronze, the strike, the air, the ear.

53
00:03:11,282 --> 00:03:14,572
The ringing is not made by
these and then sent out.

54
00:03:14,652 --> 00:03:17,874
The ringing is their
meeting, vivid and complete.

55
00:03:17,954 --> 00:03:21,216
Crack the bell, add wind, change the ear,

56
00:03:21,296 --> 00:03:23,607
and it is not the same sound altered.

57
00:03:23,687 --> 00:03:25,459
It is a different vividness.

58
00:03:26,290 --> 00:03:31,346
Verbs help. The wind is blowing: there
is no wind apart from the blowing.

59
00:03:31,426 --> 00:03:34,245
It is raining: there is no it that rains.

60
00:03:35,065 --> 00:03:38,205
Dzogchen says appearing
is spontaneous presence,

61
00:03:38,285 --> 00:03:40,338
beyond cause and effect.

62
00:03:40,418 --> 00:03:44,210
Heard with the old habits, this
swings to the other mistake.

63
00:03:44,290 --> 00:03:48,232
If appearing is not produced,
perhaps it comes from nowhere,

64
00:03:48,312 --> 00:03:49,989
or flows out of a ground.

65
00:03:50,789 --> 00:03:52,502
Keep two questions apart.

66
00:03:52,582 --> 00:03:55,763
How does this appearance come
about? Through conditions.

67
00:03:55,843 --> 00:03:57,991
What is the nature of what appears?

68
00:03:58,071 --> 00:04:02,298
Emptiness, which is not produced,
so why does not apply to it.

69
00:04:02,378 --> 00:04:05,654
Beyond cause and effect
answers the second question.

70
00:04:05,734 --> 00:04:07,697
It never cancels the first.

71
00:04:08,505 --> 00:04:11,196
Spontaneous means already complete.

72
00:04:11,276 --> 00:04:14,036
Complete because nothing
is hidden behind it,

73
00:04:14,116 --> 00:04:16,292
not because nothing conditions it.

74
00:04:16,372 --> 00:04:19,104
It is dependent arising
without a producer.

75
00:04:19,184 --> 00:04:22,569
And the last question, why
does anything appear at all,

76
00:04:22,649 --> 00:04:24,933
is not answered by a hidden source.

77
00:04:25,013 --> 00:04:27,057
It simply loses its object.

78
00:04:27,877 --> 00:04:32,403
Now the hardest part. The framework
assumes, without saying so,

79
00:04:32,483 --> 00:04:35,840
that to be present is to
be something, somewhere.

80
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:39,989
So how can something so clearly
present not be found at all?

81
00:04:40,793 --> 00:04:42,601
Do not argue from outside.

82
00:04:42,681 --> 00:04:47,031
Search exactly as the framework says
a present thing should be found.

83
00:04:47,111 --> 00:04:51,474
Is the sound in the bell? In the
air? In the ear? In the mind?

84
00:04:51,554 --> 00:04:54,014
In all of them together? Apart from them?

85
00:04:54,094 --> 00:04:57,397
Each search fails, by the
framework's own standard.

86
00:04:57,477 --> 00:05:01,179
The contradiction belongs to
the premise, not to the view.

87
00:05:01,989 --> 00:05:03,593
Each not closes a door.

88
00:05:03,673 --> 00:05:08,648
Not here, not there: here and there
are named in relation to each other.

89
00:05:08,728 --> 00:05:12,004
Not in my mind: the mind
is searched the same way,

90
00:05:12,084 --> 00:05:16,746
and is not found either. Not in
another's mind. And not even nowhere.

91
00:05:16,826 --> 00:05:22,357
Having failed to find the thing, the mind
quietly makes its absence into a place,

92
00:05:22,437 --> 00:05:24,653
a void, a background.

93
00:05:24,733 --> 00:05:28,906
But the search removes the assumed
thing and puts nothing in its place.

94
00:05:28,986 --> 00:05:34,128
Where is it, really? That question, like
the last why, has nothing left to hold.

95
00:05:34,945 --> 00:05:37,324
And this is not despite the vividness.

96
00:05:37,404 --> 00:05:40,109
If the sound had a
fixed nature of its own,

97
00:05:40,189 --> 00:05:44,240
it could not ring differently
in wind, or from a cracked bell.

98
00:05:44,320 --> 00:05:49,022
What is vivid and answers to its
conditions is exactly what cannot be found

99
00:05:49,102 --> 00:05:55,005
as a fixed thing. Vivid and not found
are one appearing, seen from two sides.

100
00:05:55,805 --> 00:05:58,795
Careful here. Emptiness
does not do anything.

101
00:05:58,875 --> 00:06:01,798
It is not a power that
makes vividness possible.

102
00:06:01,878 --> 00:06:04,466
Appearing simply never needed an essence.

103
00:06:05,289 --> 00:06:06,880
A rainbow is vivid.

104
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:10,874
Everyone sees it in the same
place, and a camera records it.

105
00:06:10,954 --> 00:06:13,551
Walk to where it is, and nothing is there.

106
00:06:13,631 --> 00:06:16,146
But the rainbow only opens the door.

107
00:06:16,226 --> 00:06:20,100
The cup, the hand and the
mind meet the same search,

108
00:06:20,180 --> 00:06:22,047
and work just as fully.

109
00:06:22,861 --> 00:06:26,816
Now the third trap, and it catches
people who have passed the first two.

110
00:06:26,896 --> 00:06:32,061
Appearing follows conditions, so surely
what is there is relations. A web.

111
00:06:32,141 --> 00:06:36,603
A network. The things are not found,
but surely the connections are.

112
00:06:37,422 --> 00:06:38,918
The tools push us here.

113
00:06:38,998 --> 00:06:44,041
Try to draw a vivid, unfindable
appearing in changing conditions.

114
00:06:44,121 --> 00:06:47,030
A diagram has only dots and lines.

115
00:06:47,110 --> 00:06:50,032
Dots for things, lines for relations.

116
00:06:50,112 --> 00:06:52,587
So it can be read only two ways.

117
00:06:52,667 --> 00:06:55,766
The dots are what is there,
and the lines join them.

118
00:06:55,846 --> 00:07:00,349
Or the lines are what is there, and
the dots are only where lines cross.

119
00:07:00,466 --> 00:07:03,787
Things as the floor, or
the web as the floor.

120
00:07:04,618 --> 00:07:06,726
The drawing does more on its own.

121
00:07:06,806 --> 00:07:09,253
It sets the conditions
around the appearance,

122
00:07:09,333 --> 00:07:11,481
so they look like outside causes.

123
00:07:11,561 --> 00:07:14,443
It holds still, so the movement is lost.

124
00:07:14,523 --> 00:07:17,188
And someone looks at the
whole web from outside.

125
00:07:17,268 --> 00:07:21,064
The onlooker that anatta took
away is quietly put back.

126
00:07:21,865 --> 00:07:25,643
Nagarjuna searched the connections
as closely as the things.

127
00:07:25,723 --> 00:07:30,508
Contact, coming into contact, and the
one who brings them into contact are not

128
00:07:30,588 --> 00:07:34,162
found. The line is as
unfindable as the dot.

129
00:07:34,242 --> 00:07:37,586
Relation and the things
related are named together,

130
00:07:37,666 --> 00:07:39,271
and neither is the ground.

131
00:07:39,351 --> 00:07:43,646
Nor is the order of conditions a
hidden set of laws behind things.

132
00:07:43,726 --> 00:07:45,508
The order is fully valid.

133
00:07:45,588 --> 00:07:49,384
It works, and it can be
relied on. It is not a floor.

134
00:07:50,202 --> 00:07:52,867
So there is no presentation free of tools.

135
00:07:52,947 --> 00:07:55,788
Every presentation picks
out this rather than that,

136
00:07:55,868 --> 00:08:00,054
so whatever it shows comes
already cut into pieces and links.

137
00:08:00,134 --> 00:08:01,984
That is not a fault to fix.

138
00:08:02,064 --> 00:08:04,620
The fix is to know it, and to say so.

139
00:08:04,700 --> 00:08:09,592
A mapmaker cannot draw a round earth
on a flat page without distortion.

140
00:08:09,672 --> 00:08:13,157
A good one says which
distortion was chosen, and why.

141
00:08:14,004 --> 00:08:16,016
Here is how to use the tools anyway.

142
00:08:16,096 --> 00:08:19,128
Say what the tool cannot
do, while using it.

143
00:08:19,208 --> 00:08:22,171
Show dependence by change, not by maps.

144
00:08:22,251 --> 00:08:25,830
Strike the bell harder,
crack it, add wind:

145
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:28,109
each time a different vividness.

146
00:08:28,189 --> 00:08:33,326
Start inside the one appearing, and
treat its conditions as its own detail.

147
00:08:33,406 --> 00:08:36,057
If you draw, then undo the drawing.

148
00:08:36,137 --> 00:08:38,204
Search a dot: not found.

149
00:08:38,284 --> 00:08:40,391
Search a line: not found.

150
00:08:40,471 --> 00:08:43,584
Search for the one looking
at the picture: not found.

151
00:08:43,664 --> 00:08:46,492
What remains is not a
blank, and not a web.

152
00:08:46,572 --> 00:08:48,439
It is the bell, ringing.

153
00:08:49,261 --> 00:08:52,469
One word carries the
whole difficulty. Real.

154
00:08:52,549 --> 00:08:57,346
It says that something works, and it
denies that anything stands on its own.

155
00:08:57,426 --> 00:08:59,643
One word for two opposite jobs.

156
00:08:59,723 --> 00:09:02,523
So say validly functioning
where it affirms,

157
00:09:02,603 --> 00:09:04,824
and not found where it denies.

158
00:09:05,633 --> 00:09:09,497
Listen to the rain again.
Vivid. Changing with the wind.

159
00:09:09,600 --> 00:09:11,191
Following its conditions.

160
00:09:11,271 --> 00:09:13,913
Not found anywhere, not even nowhere.

161
00:09:14,746 --> 00:09:19,571
The more you taste the appearances, the
more you see the nature of appearances.

162
00:09:19,651 --> 00:09:24,055
The more you see and understand the
lack and limitations of the tools,

163
00:09:24,135 --> 00:09:26,283
the clearer the mind becomes.

164
00:09:26,363 --> 00:09:29,453
And the opening turns
effortless and relaxed.

